  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1221 AM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nHot temperatures are to continue in the extended period. With \nafternoon highs in the upper 90s into the low 100s off the \ncaprock. The combined Panhandles are looking to stay under \nnorthwest to northerly flow aloft Wed onward. This is a good \nthing for precipitation prospects, as the northwest flow will help\naid in monsoonal moisture to make it to the combined Panhandles. \nAt this time, the NBM is trending upward over days three through \nfive. Different parts of the combined Panhandles will favor a 30 \nto 50 PoPs at most through each evening. To start, Wed evening the\nnorthwest is favored for storms, while the current trends in the \nforecast have the central to northeastern Panhandles favored for \nThu night. Then, for Fri evening, the NBM now has the southwest to\ncentral Panhandles with a 30 to 40 PoPs. Hard to say if these \ntrends will continue but it is promising that for at least some \nareas of the Panhandles potentially getting rain during the \nlatter part of the week.",
